  "question": {
    "text": "Among the following metals the number of metals that are extracted by self-reduction method from their respective ores is<br />\rHg, Zn, Cu, Al, Mg, Pb, Fe, Na.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Self-Reduction Process: The cations of the less electropositive metals like Pb, Hg and Cu may be reduced without the use of any additional reducing agent.<br />Self-reduction of Cu:<br /><math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />It is called self-reducing because copper oxide itself reduced the copper sulfide to give copper and sulfur dioxide.<br />Similar reactions occurs for Pb and Hg.",
    "image": null
  },
